---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../lib/url';
---

<SiteLayout current="harness-engineering" title="Harness engineering">
  <section class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Runtime discipline</p>
      <h1>Harness engineering: where agents become software.</h1>
      <p>
        Tracing tells you what happened. The harness is what makes sure
        the next run stays inside the same enforced boundaries.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="harness-map" aria-label="Agent harness responsibility map">
      <div class="harness-lane">
        <span>Inputs</span>
        <strong>User goal</strong>
        <strong>Session state</strong>
        <strong>Available tools</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="harness-core">
        <span>Harness</span>
        <h3>Controlled execution boundary</h3>
        <div>
          <strong>Build context</strong>
          <strong>Route tools</strong>
          <strong>Gate actions</strong>
          <strong>Commit events</strong>
          <strong>Stop or continue</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="harness-lane">
        <span>Outputs</span>
        <strong>Observations</strong>
        <strong>Artifacts</strong>
        <strong>Trace + eval data</strong>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="map-caption">
      Inputs flow in. The harness shapes every turn. Evidence flows out.
    </p>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 56px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">The loop</p>
      <h2>Three slots, every turn.</h2>
    </div>

    <ul class="timeline-list">
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <strong>Before the model</strong>
          <p>Load the context, assemble the instructions, and expose the available tools.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <strong>During tool execution</strong>
          <p>Enforce security policies, gate sensitive actions, and capture the tool observations.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="timeline-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <strong>After the turn</strong>
          <p>Commit state deltas, update the persistent session history, and append the trace data.</p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <div class="section-head compact-head" style="margin-top: 56px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">Where the effort moved</p>
      <h2>From <em>prompt</em> engineering to <em>context</em> engineering to <em>harness</em> engineering.</h2>
      <p>
        Each step adds a layer of control without removing the layers
        underneath. Prompts still matter; context still matters. The
        change is where the <em>load-bearing</em> work happens now — and
        which failures the team treats as engineering bugs rather than
        prompt-tuning chores.
      </p>
    </div>

    <ol class="shift-track">
      <li class="shift-stage">
        <span class="shift-stage__kicker">Stage 01</span>
        <h3>Prompt engineering</h3>
        <p class="shift-stage__lede">Tune the words you send.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>One model call, one carefully written prompt.</li>
          <li>Failures look like wording problems; fixes are edits.</li>
          <li>Caps out fast as soon as state, tools, or branches enter.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li class="shift-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 60 24" role="presentation">
          <path d="M 4 12 H 50"></path>
          <path d="M 44 6 L 54 12 L 44 18"></path>
        </svg>
      </li>
      <li class="shift-stage">
        <span class="shift-stage__kicker">Stage 02</span>
        <h3>Context engineering</h3>
        <p class="shift-stage__lede">Build the right inputs.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Retrieval, memory, tool selection, schemas, examples.</li>
          <li>Each turn assembles the context the model actually needs.</li>
          <li>Failures move from wording to <em>what the model can see</em>.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
      <li class="shift-arrow" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 60 24" role="presentation">
          <path d="M 4 12 H 50"></path>
          <path d="M 44 6 L 54 12 L 44 18"></path>
        </svg>
      </li>
      <li class="shift-stage is-now">
        <span class="shift-stage__kicker">Stage 03 · here</span>
        <h3>Harness engineering</h3>
        <p class="shift-stage__lede">Make the runtime enforce it.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Approval gates, eval files, event logs, HITL pauses, trajectory checks.</li>
          <li>Invariants live in code around the loop, not in the prompt.</li>
          <li>Failures become regressions the team can test for.</li>
        </ul>
      </li>
    </ol>

    <a class="next-card" href={url('/harness-examples/')}>
      <span>Next</span>
      <strong>See it in Google ADK</strong>
    </a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
